      "final_text_tail": "Done. Implemented template path aliasing in `src/jinja2/loaders.py`:\n\n- `BaseLoader` now has `add_alias(alias, target)`, `remove_alias(alias)` (no-op for missing aliases), and a non-recursive `_resolve_alias()` helper. Alias storage is created lazily via `__getattr__` so subclasses with their own `__init__` inherit it without modification.\n- Alias resolution is applied at the top of every `get_source` implementation (`BaseLoader`, `FileSystemLoader`, `PackageLoader`, `DictLoader`, `FunctionLoader`, `PrefixLoader`, `ChoiceLoader`) and in the overridden `load` methods (`PrefixLoader`, `ChoiceLoader`, `ModuleLoader`), so aliases resolve before normal loading and `TemplateNotFound` references the target name, not the alias.\n- No recursive chaining, overwriting aliases, and empty/special-character alias names all work; all 841 existing tests pass.",
